  "final_answer": "I have successfully found the Beginner's Spanish Specialization on Coursera and identified all the courses in it.\n\n## Beginner's Spanish Specialization on Coursera\n\n**Specialization Name**: 学习西班牙语：基本西班牙语词汇 (Learn Spanish: Basic Spanish Vocabulary)\n\n- **Provider**: University of California, Davis\n- **Instructor**: Dr. Robert Blake\n- **Level**: Beginner (初级)\n- **Rating**: 4.5 stars (5,705 reviews)\n- **Total Courses**: 5 courses\n\n### All 5 Courses in this Specialization:\n\n| # | Course Title (Chinese) | Course Title (English) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 西班牙语词汇：与人会面 | Spanish Vocabulary: Meeting People |\n| 2 | 西班牙语词汇：文化体验 | Spanish Vocabulary: Cultural Experiences |\n| 3 | 西班牙语词汇：体育、旅行和家庭 | Spanish Vocabulary: Sports, Travel, and Home |\n| 4 | 西班牙语词汇：职业和社会活动 | Spanish Vocabulary: Professions and Social Activities |\n| 5 | 西班牙语词汇项目 | Spanish Vocabulary Project |\n\nI verified the specialization by clicking on Course 1, which confirmed it is part of the \"Learn Spanish: Basic Spanish Vocabulary\" Specialization (the URL contained `specialization=learn-spanish`). Each course builds on vocabulary skills, starting with basic meeting vocabulary and progressing through cultural, sports/travel/home, and professional/social contexts, culminating in a final project course.",
